Package: @PACKAGE@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: nodejs (>= @NODE_MIN@), libc6 (>= 2.35)
Recommends: git
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness
Conflicts: dsh
Replaces: dsh
X-DSH-Source-Ref: @DSH_REF@
X-DSH-Source-Commit: @DSH_COMMIT@
X-DSH-Bundled-Pnpm: @PNPM_VERSION@
Description: DeepSeek Harness Web UI and CLI (dsh)
 DeepSeek Harness is an open-source agent harness from DeepSeek AI, built on
 an everything-is-a-plugin architecture (Cordis).
 .
 This package installs the `dsh` command and the Web UI under /usr/lib/dsh,
 plus a systemd *user* unit, dsh-web.service. The service runs as the
 logged-in user, keeps its state in that user's ~/.dsh, and serves the Web UI
 at http://127.0.0.1:3080. No root system service is installed or enabled.
 .
 The package depends on the system Node.js (>= 24.9.0); it does not bundle a
 runtime. On Ubuntu 24.04, install Node 24 from NodeSource first.
 .
 Plugin management (`dsh plugin` and the Web Plugins page) uses the bundled
 pnpm @PNPM_VERSION@ under /usr/lib/dsh/pnpm; no separate pnpm install is
 needed. Plugins themselves are per user and live in ~/.dsh, not in this
 package.
 .
 The package name is deepseek-harness because the unrelated Debian/Ubuntu
 package `dsh` (distributed shell) already owns that name and /usr/bin/dsh;
 the two packages conflict.
